        cout << "NO\n";
    } else {
        if (canPartition(a, 0, m)) {
            cout << "YES\n";
        } else {
            cout << "NO\n";
        }
    }

    return 0;
}
```

This solution uses dynamic programming to determine if there exists a subset of the array that sums up to half of the total sum. If such a subset exists, it means the array can be divided into two parts with equal sum, and the answer is "YES". Otherwise, the answer is "NO". The time complexity of this solution is O(n * m), which is efficient given the constraints. 

To verify the correctness of the solution, you can test it with various inputs, including edge cases like an array with all elements being the same or an array where no partitioning is possible. This ensures the solution handles all specified requirements accurately. 

Note: The solution assumes that the input values are within the range that can be handled by the data types used in the code. If necessary, adjustments should be made to handle larger values or specific constraints. 

This approach effectively solves the problem while adhering to the guidelines provided. 

