s[i] is either '0' or '1'.

```
class Solution {
public:
    int minFlipsMonoIncr(string S) {
        int n = S.size();
        vector<int> dp(n+1, 0);

        for(int i=1; i<=n; i++){
            if(S[i-1] == '1')
                dp[i] = dp[i-1]+1;
            else
                dp[i] = min(dp[i-1], i-dp[i-1]-1);
        }

        return dp[n];
    }
};
```


**dp[i]**: minimum flips to make the first **i** characters monotonic increasing. 

If **S[i-1] == '1'**, then we need to flip all previous '0's to '1', so it is **dp[i] = dp[i-1]+1**.

Otherwise, we have two options:

1. Keep **S[i-1] == '0'**, then we need to flip all previous '1's to '0', which is **i-dp[i-1]-1** (all previous characters minus the number of previous '0's)
2. Flip **S[i-1] == '1'**, then we need to flip **dp[i-1]** times. Since we flip **S[i-1]**, we don't need to flip any previous characters anymore, so the result is still **dp[i-1]**. So this option is **dp[i-1]**. 

The final result is the minimum of these two options. So it is **dp[i] = min(dp[i-1], i-dp[i-1]-1)**. 

Time complexity: O(n)
Space complexity: O(n) but can be optimized to O(1) by using only two variables. 

