    std::vector<std::vector<int>> result(n, std::vector<int>(n, 0));

    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        result[i][i] = 1;
    }

    return result;
}
```

This version makes it explicit that all elements are initialized to zero before setting the diagonal elements to one. However, the previous version without the explicit initialization is generally more efficient and concise. 

