**Answer:**
To create a custom `TextRenderer` in JavaFX that supports both HTML and plain text rendering, you can extend the `TextRenderer` class provided by the Apache POI library. Here's an example of how you can implement this:

```java
import org.apache.poi.xslf.usermodel.XMLSlideShow;
import org.apache.poi.xslf.usermodel.XSLFTextParagraph;
import org.apache.poi.xslf.usermodel.XSLFTextRun;

public class CustomTextRenderer extends TextRenderer {

    public CustomTextRenderer(XMLSlideShow ppt) {
        super(ppt);
    }

    @Override
    protected void renderHtml(String html, XSLFTextParagraph p, XSLFTextRun run) {
        // Custom HTML rendering logic here
        // For example, you can use a library like Jsoup to parse and render HTML
